# QM-region extraction for the VERIFIED TS geometry (COMPUTATIONAL.md C8).
#
# The verified TS is ../verify_exact_hessian/job.xyz -- the geometry whose exact
# NumFreq gave one imaginary mode at -576.3 cm-1. It is copied here verbatim.
# ../job.xyz must NOT be used as the TS: it was overwritten by a crashed OptTS
# attempt and is a DIFFERENT structure (RMSD 0.447 A, O136-C129 2.596 vs the
# verified 1.820 A). ../job.QMRegion.xyz was checked atom-by-atom against both
# geometries and belongs to the bad one (its O136-C129 is 2.596 A), so it cannot
# seed the composite correction either.
#
# A plain single point does NOT emit job.QMRegion.xyz, so this is a one-cycle
# optimisation purely to make ORCA write it (MaxIter 1, no freq -- the geometry
# must not be allowed to leave the saddle). The QM/MM block is identical to
# ../verify_exact_hessian/job.inp (same 20-atom QM region, same GFNFF topology
# convention, charge 0), so the extracted 22-atom fragment (20 QM + 2 link H)
# is the one the composite correction needs.
! QM/XTB r2SCAN-3c ddCOSMO(Water) opt TightSCF

%QMMM
QMATOMS
	{61 64 120 121 122 124 125 126 128 129 130 131 132 133 134 135 136 137 138 139}
END
Charge_total 0
Mult_total 1
AutoFF_QM2_Method GFNFF
END

%geom
MaxIter 1
END

%output jsonpropfile true end

%maxcore 4000

%pal
   nprocs 8
end

* xyzfile 0 1 job.xyz
